{{also|Salmon|salmón}}
==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
{{dercat|en|cel|qfa-sub}}
From {{inh|en|enm|samoun}}, {{m|enm|samon}}, {{m|enm|saumon}}, from {{der|en|xno|saumon}}, from {{der|en|fro|saumon}}, from {{der|en|la|salmo|salmō, salmōn-}}. Widely displaced native {{cog|enm|lax}}, from {{cog|ang|leax|}} (whence modern dialectal {{m|en|lax}}). The unpronounced ''l'' was later inserted to make the word appear closer to its Latin root (compare words like {{m|en|debt}}, {{m|en|indict}}, {{m|en|receipt}} for the same spelling Latinizations).

The verb sense {{m-g|ride a bicycle the wrong way down a one-way street}} alludes to salmon swimming upstream against the flow of a river to spawn.

