===Noun===
{{en-noun|~|salmon|salmons}}

# {{senseid|en|Q2796766}}{{lb|en|fish}} One of [[several]] [[species]] of [[fish]], typically of the {{taxfmt|Salmoninae|subfamily}} subfamily, brownish above with silvery sides and delicate pinkish-orange flesh; they ascend rivers to [[spawn]].
#: {{coi|en|grilled '''salmon'''}}
#: {{coi|en|'''salmon''' paté}}
#: {{coi|en|'''salmon''' steak}}
#: {{syn|en|lax|lox}}
# A [[meal]] or [[dish]] made from this fish.
# {{qualifier|plural '''salmons'''}} A pale [[pinkish]]-[[orange]] [[colour]], the colour of cooked salmon.
#: {{syn|en|salmon pink}}
#: {{color panel|FA8072}}
# The upper [[brick]]s in a [[kiln]] which receive the least [[heat]].
# {{lb|en|Cockney rhyming slang}} [[snout]] (tobacco; from ''salmon and trout'')
#* {{quote-song|en|year=1992|artist={{w|The Shamen}}|title=w:Ebeneezer Goode|passage=Got any '''salmon'''?}}

